<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Savonia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Savo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Savonia, Savo in Finnish, is a historical province of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>, a landscape of lakes and forests around Mikkeli and Kuopio. Its people practised slash-and-burn farming and spread far beyond the province, settling in central Finland, Värmland in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ingria">Ingria</a>. It was long a frontier of the Swedish realm facing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and was crossed by wars into the 18th century.</p></div>
